Rewritten for Nodecode: the provider profile (its id, display name, base URL,
key variables, signup page and fallback model list), its rule that a
reasoning model is offered the relay's whole OpenAI-compatible wire vocabulary
rather than a per-model subset, and its rule that a round nobody set an effort
on is sent medium instead of inheriting the relay's ceiling - here the
section's `default_effort`, which an operator may move or set to "endpoint".
The model list is read on demand by the `/crowbot` command rather than at
load: GET /models names ids only, so each one is offered with the section's
context window and the whole ladder, and nothing is cached across keys beyond
the one last read. Left out: the Hermes ProviderProfile class and the
reasoning-config object it answers, whose `enabled`/`effort` pair Nodecode
spells as the effort rung itself (`off` or a rung); the provider aliases,
because Nodecode's picker reads one provider id; and the legacy
`HERMES_CUSTOM_API_CROWBOT_SH_API_KEY` variable, which is still read here so
an existing install keeps working.
